## Summary

I verified every claim against the tree before writing anything. Only one issue had real news.

#716 — commented + closed. Genuinely fixed this session.
• 9e29257 adds pure spawn_dir_restrictions(parent, worktree), wired at both call sites the issue named (handle_spawn:822, handle_spawn_bg:970). Three new tests, all passing (verified by running them, not assuming).
• The enforcement path already existed — `maybe_guard/maybe_guard_arc in tools::build_tools consult dir_restrictions, and check_path short-circuits to Ok` on an empty ruleset, which is precisely why cloning an empty parent gave zero confinement.
• b542e4a retracts the CLAUDE.md over-promise the issue flagged.
• I disclosed two limits rather than claiming a clean win: bash with a non-git absolute path still escapes, and the allow list **narrows reads** too — a worker's read_file outside the worktree now fails where it used to succeed. That's a real behavior change, not free.

